{"id": "ch19", "number": "19", "title": "Additional rules for TFL", "titleInlines": [{"type": "text", "text": "Additional rules for TFL"}], "part": "IV", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "In "}, {"type": "ref", "label": "s:BasicTFL", "variant": "cref", "href": "/read/ch17", "text": "chapter 17"}, {"type": "text", "text": ", we introduced the basic rules of our proof system for TFL. In this section, we will add some additional rules to our system. Our extended proof system is a bit easier to work with. (However, in "}, {"type": "ref", "label": "s:Derived", "variant": "cref", "href": "/read/ch21", "text": "chapter 21"}, {"type": "text", "text": " we will see that they are not strictly speaking "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "necessary"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ".)"}]}, {"type": "heading", "level": 2, "number": "19.1", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Disjunctive syllogism"}], "id": "sec-19-1"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here is a very natural argument form."}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "earg", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Elizabeth is either in Massachusetts or in DC."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "She is not in DC."}]}]}, {"label": [{"type": "text", "text": "∴"}], "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "She is in Massachusetts."}]}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is called "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "disjunctive syllogism"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". We add it to our proof system as follows:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{A} \\lor \\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "n", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{A}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{B}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "DS"}], "refs": "m, n", "ruleText": "DS"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "and"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{A} \\lor \\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "n", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{A}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "DS"}], "refs": "m, n", "ruleText": "DS"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "As usual, the disjunction and the negation of one disjunct may occur in either order and need not be adjacent. However, we always cite the disjunction first."}]}, {"type": "heading", "level": 2, "number": "19.2", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Modus tollens"}], "id": "sec-19-2"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Another useful pattern of inference is embodied in the following argument:"}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "earg", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "If Hilary has won the election, then she is in the White House."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "She is not in the White House."}]}]}, {"label": [{"type": "text", "text": "∴"}], "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "She has not won the election."}]}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This inference pattern is called "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "modus tollens"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". The corresponding rule is:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{A}\\rightarrow \\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "n", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{A}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "MT"}], "refs": "m, n", "ruleText": "MT"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "As usual, the premises may occur in either order, but we always cite the conditional first."}]}, {"type": "heading", "level": 2, "number": "19.3", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Double-negation elimination"}], "id": "sec-19-3"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Another useful rule is "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "double-negation elimination"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". It does exactly what it says on the tin:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\lnot \\mathcal{A}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{A}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "DNE"}], "refs": "m", "ruleText": "DNE"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The justification for this is that, in natural language, double-negations tend to cancel out."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "That said, you should be aware that context and emphasis can prevent them from doing so. Consider: ‘Jane is not "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "not"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " happy’. Arguably, one cannot infer ‘Jane is happy’, since the first sentence should be understood as meaning the same as ‘Jane is not "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "un"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "happy’. This is compatible with ‘Jane is in a state of profound indifference’. As usual, moving to TFL forces us to sacrifice certain nuances of English expressions."}]}, {"type": "heading", "level": 2, "number": "19.4", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Excluded middle"}], "id": "sec-19-4"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Suppose that we can show that if it’s sunny outside, then Bill will have brought an umbrella (for fear of burning). Suppose we can also show that, if it’s not sunny outside, then Bill will have brought an umbrella (for fear of rain). Well, there is no third way for the weather to be. So, "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "whatever the weather"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", Bill will have brought an umbrella."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This line of thinking motivates the following rule:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "i", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\mathcal{A}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "j", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "k", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{A}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "l", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\mathcal{B}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "LEM"}], "refs": "i–j, k–l", "ruleText": "LEM"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The rule is sometimes called the "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "rule of excluded middle"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". You can think of it as "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\lor", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "E applied to "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\mathcal{A} \\lor \\lnot \\mathcal{A}", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ". There can be as many lines as you like between "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "i", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "j", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", and as many lines as you like between "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "k", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "l", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ". Moreover, the subproofs can come in any order, and the second subproof does not need to come immediately after the first."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "To see the rule in action, consider:"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "P \\therefore (P \\land D) \\lor (P \\land \\lnot D)"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here is a proof corresponding with the argument:"}]}, {"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "P", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "PR"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "PR"}, {"num": "2", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "D", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "3", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "P \\land D", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\land"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "1, 2", "ruleText": "∧I"}, {"num": "4", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "(P \\land D) \\lor (P \\land \\lnot D)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lor"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "3", "ruleText": "∨I"}, {"num": "5", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot D", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "6", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "P \\land \\lnot D", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\land"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "1, 5", "ruleText": "∧I"}, {"num": "7", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "(P \\land D) \\lor (P \\land \\lnot D)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lor"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "6", "ruleText": "∨I"}, {"num": "8", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "(P \\land D) \\lor (P \\land \\lnot D)", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "LEM"}], "refs": "2–4, 5–7", "ruleText": "LEM"}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here is another example:"}]}, {"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "A \\rightarrow \\lnot A", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "PR"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "PR"}, {"num": "2", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "A", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "3", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot A", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\rightarrow"}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "1, 2", "ruleText": "→E"}, {"num": "4", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot A", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "5", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot A", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "R"}], "refs": "4", "ruleText": "R"}, {"num": "6", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot A", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "LEM"}], "refs": "2–3, 4–5", "ruleText": "LEM"}]}, {"type": "heading", "level": 2, "number": "19.5", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "De Morgan Rules"}], "id": "sec-19-5"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Our final additional rules are called De Morgan’s Laws (named after Augustus De Morgan). The shape of the rules should be familiar from truth tables."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The first De Morgan rule is:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot (\\mathcal{A} \\land \\mathcal{B})", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{A} \\lor \\lnot \\mathcal{B}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "DeM"}], "refs": "m", "ruleText": "DeM"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The second De Morgan is the reverse of the first:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{A} \\lor \\lnot \\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot (\\mathcal{A} \\land \\mathcal{B})", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "DeM"}], "refs": "m", "ruleText": "DeM"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The third De Morgan rule is the "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "dual"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " of the first:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot (\\mathcal{A} \\lor \\mathcal{B})", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{A} \\land \\lnot \\mathcal{B}", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "DeM"}], "refs": "m", "ruleText": "DeM"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "And the fourth is the reverse of the third:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\mathcal{A} \\land \\lnot \\mathcal{B}", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot (\\mathcal{A} \\lor \\mathcal{B})", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "DeM"}], "refs": "m", "ruleText": "DeM"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "These are all of the additional rules of our proof system for TFL."}]}]}], "exercises": [{"letter": "A", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The following proofs are missing their citations (rule and line numbers). Add them wherever they are required:"}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "compactlist", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "W \\rightarrow \\lnot B", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "2", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "A \\land W", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "3", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "B \\lor (J \\land K)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "4", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "W", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "5", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot B", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "6", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "J \\land K", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "7", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "K", "rule": null, "refs": null}]}], "id": "ch19.A.1", "formulas": []}, {"children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "L \\leftrightarrow \\lnot O", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "2", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "L \\lor \\lnot O", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "3", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot L", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "4", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot O", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "5", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "L", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "6", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "7", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\lnot L", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "8", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "L", "rule": null, "refs": null}]}], "id": "ch19.A.2", "formulas": []}, {"children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "Z \\rightarrow (C \\land \\lnot N)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "2", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot Z \\rightarrow (N \\land \\lnot C)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "3", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot (N \\lor C)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "4", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot N \\land \\lnot C", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "5", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot N", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "6", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot C", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "7", "depth": 2, "hypo": true, "formula": "Z", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "8", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "C \\land \\lnot N", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "9", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "C", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "10", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "11", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot Z", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "12", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "N \\land \\lnot C", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "13", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "N", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "14", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "15", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\lnot (N \\lor C)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "16", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "N \\lor C", "rule": null, "refs": null}]}], "id": "ch19.A.3", "formulas": []}]}], "items": [{"children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "W \\rightarrow \\lnot B", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "2", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "A \\land W", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "3", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "B \\lor (J \\land K)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "4", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "W", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "5", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot B", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "6", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "J \\land K", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "7", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "K", "rule": null, "refs": null}]}], "id": "ch19.A.1", "formulas": []}, {"children": [{"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "L \\leftrightarrow \\lnot O", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "2", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "L \\lor \\lnot O", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "3", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot L", "rule": nu